WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
Normal clotting confines fibrin
formation to a vessel injury.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.298
This scholarly repair figure provides the reference.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.240
Disseminated intravascular coagulation changes
the location and extent of

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:11.891
that process.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.000
In DIC, widespread tissue
factor exposure activates clotting.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.422
Thrombin and fibrin activity increase.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.760
Fibrin deposits inside small
vessels impede blood flow, reducing

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:23.716
organ perfusion.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.962
As clotting continues, platelets
and coagulation factors are consumed.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.417
Accelerated fibrinolysis accompanies the process.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.767
The same patient can
therefore have microvascular thrombosis and

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:36.600
uncontrolled bleeding.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.916
Treatment goals include eliminating
the underlying pathology, restoring hemostasis

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.583
and supporting failing organs.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.163
Component replacement alone does
not remove the trigger.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.372
Chapter twenty nine, slides
one hundred seventeen through one

00:00:51.372 --> 00:00:53.178
hundred twenty, support this sequence.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:58.140
The complete diagnostic laboratory
pattern and specific treatment indications

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.765
remain textbook gaps.
